WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.902
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Tom Hanks.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.237
You are a man who wears --
-I love that rhythm section.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.638
-They're very good over there.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.540
You're a man of many hats
but one thing that I keep

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.375
sort of seeing popping up
over social media

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:12.445
over the last few years is
that you are a man who will

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:16.749
show up at a wedding,
invited or not.

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:18.350
-I tell ya.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.186
It's my ego unchecked.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.789
I just can't help but think,
"What would these people

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:27.259
like more than anything else to
remember this magic day of days?

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:30.130
Oh, I know. Me."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.997
So I've crashed another one.

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:33.299
-So, Rome, you crashed one
in Rome.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.768
-Okay, now, this is important
because Ron --

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:38.504
-This is "Angels &amp; Demons."
-Ron Howard and I, we were

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:40.940
making one of those fabulous
Robert Langdon movies,

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.008
and I hope he asks me
to do 19 more

00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:45.044
because they are a blast.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.812
[ Applause ]
Thank you, yeah.

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:49.048
So, the problem here,

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:52.085
we were shooting in right
in front of the Pantheon.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.920
And I'm talking about
the Pantheon.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.989
This is a building that was --
you know, it says

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.825
"Marcus Agrippa" on it,
for crying --

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.326
That's who built the thing.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.728
Somebody tell me
when Marcus Agrippa died.

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:04.363
I'll tell you when.

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:07.033
A thousand years before --
I don't know when he died,

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.235
but it is now also
a Catholic church.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.137
It is a consecrated
Catholic church.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.406
So we were shooting in front of
it, and lo and behold,

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.541
they had booked a wedding in
there while we're shooting stuff

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:18.210
with trucks, and, you know,
me and Ayelet Zurer

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.613
are running around, trying to
solve the great mysteries.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:24.417
And this limousine pulled up,
and it was the bride

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.885
and the groom trying to get --

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.021
♪ Get me to the church on time ♪

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.890
And they couldn't do it because
we had all this stuff going on.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.058
It was like,
"Uh, how do we fix this?"

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:35.128
So, like --
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:39.132
Like a stalker, you know,
"Hey, miss, miss, miss,"

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.700
I knocked on the window and
said, "Listen, we have a thing

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.269
in there, but would you do me
the honor of escorting you

00:01:44.269 --> 00:01:45.938
to your bridal altar?"

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:49.775
So we did it. And then that's
the bride and her dad,

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:50.844
and we got her to the church.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:52.278
-They knew who you were
right away?

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:55.648
-I'm not so sure because they
might not have because I had

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.082
that chemically straightened
hair,

00:01:57.082 --> 00:01:59.118
as you can see right there,
which is a little different.

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:01.654
-You look a little bit like
a Tom Hanks impersonator.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.123
-I might have been
a guy trying to get --

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:05.458
[ Italian accent ]
"For a mere five euros,

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.893
you can take your picture
with me."

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:09.261
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:11.097
-[ Italian accent ] "This is me
from 'Big,' Tom Hanks."

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:13.766
-[ Normal voice ] That was one
of the first times.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.336
I don't like to think
I crashed a wedding.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.838
I sort of provided a service.
-You did.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.639
But you got a taste of it.

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:23.208
-Oh, well, then --
What's more exciting?

00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:24.443
-So what's going on here?

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:27.947
-Okay, alright, this is --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.683
Okay, this is in the fabulous
city of Pittsburgh.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.017
-The Burgh!
-The Burgh,

00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:33.819
the Manhattan
on the Monongahela,

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:36.588
the Athens of the Allegheny,
the Oslo of the Ohio,

00:02:36.588 --> 00:02:38.024
the City of Three Rivers.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.760
And Rita and I, we going off
for a walk

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.428
somewhere on on our day off.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:45.297
And just as we were getting into
our car, in the condominium part

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:47.833
of the building, this wedding
party was coming up

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:51.804
to get into the biggest cocktail
booze-cruise bus I'd ever seen.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.539
[ Laughter ]
So they were they were all go--

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:56.242
I mean, look, there's 47.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.811
There are less
Pittsburgh Steelers

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:02.214
than there are bridesmaids
in this photograph.

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:04.417
And we said, "Oh, it looks like,
oh, the matching dresses.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.385
It must be bridesmaids.
Well, if the bride comes out,

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:07.486
I jump out and take a picture.

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:09.254
♪ Well, dun dun-dun
dun-dun duh ♪

00:03:09.254 --> 00:03:13.792
She shows up. So, yes,
I crashed their wedding photo.

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:16.029
-But then you --
Now, before I show it,

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.931
this is you answered a request.
-Yes. Yes.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.832
-Okay. Because this one
does not look --

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.400
This would not be okay
if you just showed up.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.702
-I did not crash that wedding.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:25.271
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:28.007
These were folks -- We were
actually shooting a movie

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.208
called "A Man Called Otto."

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:30.743
And we were shooting
in Pittsburgh.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:34.013
And our base camp, a buttress
to these folks, is property.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:36.215
And they had a couple kids.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:37.683
There's one of their kids
right there.

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.252
And they said, "Look, we've been
thinking about getting married.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.586
We couldn't figure out
how to do it."

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:43.556
And they said, "If you got a day
off, could you marry us?"

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:44.991
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:49.028
And I'd like to have you know
that as an ordained minister

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.297
of the Universal Life Church --
-Yeah, okay.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.365
What do you pay for a license
like that?

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:56.969
-I'd like to think I studied
the gospels for over $35.

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:58.604
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.604 --> 00:03:59.839
-That's a different thing.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:03.375
So by the by the commonwealth of
Pennsylvania,

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:06.478
or is it state of Pennsylvania,
I could perform this wedding.

00:04:06.478 --> 00:04:11.250
And I did.
It was Krisna and her old man,

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.618
as I like to call him.

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:16.788
And they had sort of --
I had a couple words to say.

00:04:16.788 --> 00:04:19.492
They wrote their vows, and it
was absolutely beautiful.

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.394
And it was a great honor.
-It's an incredible --

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.128
That's an incredible thing that
you did that for them.

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:24.630
I would imagine,
much like Memphis,

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.032
after playing Mr. Rogers
and doing a few movies there,

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:30.369
you probably can't pay
for a beer in Pittsburgh either.

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:33.206
-No, actually, I can.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:36.642
Because what I get is, I get
the check and a hearty thanks

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:38.211
for all I've done for the city
of Pittsburgh.

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:39.645
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:41.647
-It's a different place.

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.949
-I got to tell you,
Pittsburgh is a place --

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:45.852
No one leaves Pittsburgh.
-Yeah.

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:47.820
-They love living in Pittsburgh.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.855
They have great, great,
great, great pride,

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:52.225
and no small amount of "Hey,
man, thanks for being here."

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:55.294
Not more than that.
-Yeah, I will say, you might not

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:57.497
remember, the last time I saw
you was on the set of

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:58.797
"Won't You Be My Neighbor?"

00:04:58.797 --> 00:05:00.833
You were filming.
My dad is from Pittsburgh,

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:03.736
and he used to go and sit in
the audience in that studio,

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.004
because you filmed it
in the exact studio.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.505
-At WQED.

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:08.173
-And we were lucky enough
to stop by.

00:05:08.173 --> 00:05:10.809
And it was a real trip for me,
but it was really --

00:05:10.809 --> 00:05:13.379
It was special for him.
We really appreciated that.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.447
-That was a walk through
the time-space continuum

00:05:15.447 --> 00:05:17.150
on that one there, yeah.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.684
Oh, I don't know if I told this.

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:20.853
You're in Pittsburgh,
and I'm going up the elevator.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.155
Everybody knows
where they're shooting

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:24.323
the Mr. Rogers movie, right?

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:27.059
And it's at the end of the day,
I'm going up in the el,

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:29.795
I'm in my sweats and stuff,
and a Pittsburghian

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:32.231
gets in the elevator, because
there's a big, you know,

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:34.801
rooftop wingding thing that's
going on there where we are.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.503
He's like, "You're Tom Hanks,
aren't you?"

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.005
Said, "Yeah, yeah. How are you?"

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:41.073
"Ooh.

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:42.341
How's filming going?"

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:43.776
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.911
And I said, "You know, it's
actually going pretty well."

00:05:45.911 --> 00:05:48.314
Said, "Mm-hmm. Is the city
treating you properly?"

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:50.349
I said, "Yeah, yeah,
Pittsburgh's doing us

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:51.817
a pretty good solid, thank you."

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:53.152
"Well, good luck to you."

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:56.188
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:57.890
"I hope it goes well."

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.926
And just before I get out of the
elevator, he turns and he leans

00:06:00.926 --> 00:06:02.328
through it
as the doors are closing.

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:04.263
He leans over and says,
"We take Mr. Rogers

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.966
very seriously in this town."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.401
-I like it.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:11.137
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:13.373
I just really --

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:15.374
I really like that he was
worried Tom Hanks

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:16.876
was gonna do a hit job.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.679
-Uh, let's understand, as I say,

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:21.714
they're very proud of their town
there in Pittsburgh.

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:24.450
They don't want some interloper
coming in and mucking things up.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.418
-Well, you did not,
in that case.

00:06:26.418 --> 00:06:29.722
And I've heard, all the people
whose weddings

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:32.058
you've participated in are
very still happily married.

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:34.560
-Yeah, there you go.
How about that?

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.095
I think a little fairy dust has

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:37.864
been sprinkled
upon the altar there.

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:39.097
-Hey, congrats on the movie.

00:06:39.097 --> 00:06:40.633
Thank you so much for making
the time for us.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.201
It is so wonderful at last.

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:44.170
That's Tom Hanks!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.406
"Elvis" will be in theaters
June 24th.

